{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"06bfd6378a113910","name":"card_unit_6th_motor_rifles","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Allegiance/units/card_unit_6th_motor_rifles","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"15th MOTOR RIFLES","text":"Your HQ is immune to damage on enemy turns.","flavorText":"The 15th Guards Rifle Regiment became part of the 2nd Guards RIfle Division in its second formation in 1942. After participating in the Novorossiysk-Taman offensive in 1943 the division was renamed to 2nd Guards (Tamanskaya) Motor Rifle Division and that same year it was under the command of the 56th Army in the Kerch-Eltigen Operation. In 1944 the division participated in the Crimean Offensive under the command of the Separate Coastal Army, and after that it was held in reserve with the 2nd Guards Army, or until July 1944 when the whole army was moved to the 1st Baltic Front. The division fought in the Battle of Memel in 1944 before it was transferred to the 3rd Belorussian Front to participate in the East Prussian offensive. When the war ended the 2nd Guards Motor Rifle Division was located in the Baltic Sea coast north of Primorsk.","faction":"Soviet","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_6th_motor_rifles","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_6th_motor_rifles_title","SourceString":"15th MOTOR RIFLES","LocalizedString":"15th MOTOR RIFLES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_6th_motor_rifles_text","SourceString":"Your HQ is immune to damage on enemy turns.","LocalizedString":"Your HQ is immune to damage on enemy turns."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_6th_motor_rifles_history","SourceString":"The 15th Guards Rifle Regiment became part of the 2nd Guards RIfle Division in its second formation in 1942. After participating in the Novorossiysk-Taman offensive in 1943 the division was renamed to 2nd Guards (Tamanskaya) Motor Rifle Division and that same year it was under the command of the 56th Army in the Kerch-Eltigen Operation. In 1944 the division participated in the Crimean Offensive under the command of the Separate Coastal Army, and after that it was held in reserve with the 2nd Guards Army, or until July 1944 when the whole army was moved to the 1st Baltic Front. The division fought in the Battle of Memel in 1944 before it was transferred to the 3rd Belorussian Front to participate in the East Prussian offensive. When the war ended the 2nd Guards Motor Rifle Division was located in the Baltic Sea coast north of Primorsk.","LocalizedString":"The 15th Guards Rifle Regiment became part of the 2nd Guards RIfle Division in its second formation in 1942. After participating in the Novorossiysk-Taman offensive in 1943 the division was renamed to 2nd Guards (Tamanskaya) Motor Rifle Division and that same year it was under the command of the 56th Army in the Kerch-Eltigen Operation. In 1944 the division participated in the Crimean Offensive under the command of the Separate Coastal Army, and after that it was held in reserve with the 2nd Guards Army, or until July 1944 when the whole army was moved to the 1st Baltic Front. The division fought in the Battle of Memel in 1944 before it was transferred to the 3rd Belorussian Front to participate in the East Prussian offensive. When the war ended the 2nd Guards Motor Rifle Division was located in the Baltic Sea coast north of Primorsk."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isInPermanentPool":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeStartOfTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Immune"],"hasGuard":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Infantry_Move